  PCSX2 (https://github.com/PCSX2/pcsx2, GPL-3.0-or-later), Qiita by
  kazuhidet (https://qiita.com/kazuhidet/items/849c259f57e51ab32ab6, no
  license published), RPCS3 (https://github.com/RPCS3/rpcs3, GPL-2.0),
  Scrapbox by p4ken (https://scrapbox.io/p4ken/, no license published) and
  Train Controller Database
  (https://github.com/marcriera/train-controller-db, no license published).
  TritonLib and SteamHapticsPlayer (https://github.com/Pixel1011/TritonLib,
  https://github.com/Pixel1011/SteamHapticsPlayer, Apache-2.0),
  steam-controller-live-haptics
  (https://github.com/FamBoy32-dev/steam-controller-live-haptics, MIT),
  steam-controller-stuff (https://github.com/iczero/steam-controller-stuff,
  MIT) and sc2ds (https://github.com/ga2mer/sc2ds, no license published):
  the Steam Controller 2026 PCM haptics stream, reports 0x86, 0x88 and
  0x44.
  ViGEmClient (https://github.com/nefarius/ViGEmClient, MIT): the
  DS4_REPORT_EX layout behind the virtual DualShock 4 input report.
  VIIPER, hbashton fork (https://github.com/hbashton/VIIPER, GPL-3.0): the
  virtual DualSense microphone's 48 dB attenuation range.
  Wheel protocol references: native Fanatec, Thrustmaster and Logitech force
  feedback and RPM shift LED reports, read from hid-fanatecff
  (https://github.com/gotzl/hid-fanatecff, GPL-2.0), hid-tmff2
  (https://github.com/Kimplul/hid-tmff2, GPL-2.0-or-later), new-lg4ff
  (https://github.com/berarma/new-lg4ff, GPL-2.0), oversteer
  (https://github.com/berarma/oversteer, GPL-3.0) and thrustmaster-led-linux
  (https://github.com/wKoja/thrustmaster-led-linux, GPL-3.0), and
  cross-checked against the SimHub Thrustmaster Wheel LED Controller
  (https://gitlab.com/prodigal.knight/simhub-thrustmaster-wheel-led-controller,
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2023 Prodigal.Knight) and tm-bt-led
  (https://github.com/mplutka/tm-bt-led, MIT, Copyright 2020 Markus Plutka).
  WiiBrew (https://wiibrew.org/wiki/Wiimote, no license published): the Wii
  Remote speaker protocol, the 8-bit PCM configuration and the IR
  calibration block.
  WiimoteLib (https://github.com/BrianPeek/WiimoteLib, MIT): Wii IR
  camera and Balance Board behavior.
  X1nput (https://github.com/araghon007/X1nput, MIT): the Xbox
  impulse-trigger 9-byte report and its write path.
  Xbox controller references: the protocols behind the SDL fork's original
  Xbox, Steel Battalion, Xbox 360 chatpad and Xbox 360 uDraw drivers, and
  the Xbox 360 receivers PadForge binds to Windows' own driver, read from
  brandonw.net (https://brandonw.net/udraw/, no license published), Chatpad
  Super Driver (https://github.com/GAFBlizzard/chatpad-super-driver, MIT),
  Cxbx-Reloaded (https://github.com/Cxbx-Reloaded/Cxbx-Reloaded,
  GPL-2.0-or-later), euc.jp by ITO Takayuki
  (http://euc.jp/periphs/xbox-controller.en.html, all rights reserved, read
  through the Wayback Machine), JoypadOS
  (https://github.com/joypad-ai/joypad-os, Apache-2.0), libSteelBattalion
  (https://github.com/faha223/libSteelBattalion, no license published),
  libsteelbat (https://github.com/qdot/libsteelbat, no license published),
  Linux kernel (https://github.com/torvalds/linux, GPL-2.0), ogx360
  (https://github.com/Ryzee119/ogx360, GPL-3.0-or-later), s-config.com
  (https://www.s-config.com/, no license published), SBC
  (https://github.com/SantiagoSaldana/SBC, MIT in its license file and
  headers, LGPL-2.1-or-later in its readme), Spivey's Corner
  (https://spivey.oriel.ox.ac.uk/corner/Notes_on_the_XBox360_chatpad, no
  license published), steel-battalion-net
  (https://github.com/jcoutch/steel-battalion-net, LGPL-3.0 text,
  GPL-3.0-or-later file headers), SteelBattalionController
  (https://github.com/faha223/SteelBattalionController, Apache-2.0),
  SteelBattalionDriver (https://github.com/caosdoar/SteelBattalionDriver,
  GPL-3.0), SteelBattalionMapper
  (https://github.com/Shopcreeper/SteelBattalionMapper, GPL-3.0-or-later),
  tusb_xinput (https://github.com/Ryzee119/tusb_xinput, MIT, with its
  JoypadOS fork at https://github.com/joypad-ai/tusb_xinput, MIT),
  uDrawTablet (https://github.com/brandonlw/uDrawTablet, no license
  published), Xb2XInput (https://github.com/emoose/Xb2XInput, GPL-3.0),
  xb360ChatpadToKM (https://github.com/jackdarker/xb360ChatpadToKM,
  GPL-3.0), xbox360wirelesschatpad
  (https://github.com/Kytech/xbox360wirelesschatpad, a warranty disclaimer,
  no license grant), xboxdevwiki
  (https://xboxdevwiki.net/Xbox_Input_Devices, no license published),
  xboxdrv (https://github.com/xboxdrv/xboxdrv, GPL-3.0-or-later) and xemu
  (https://github.com/xemu-project/xemu, LGPL-2.0-or-later).
  xone and xow (https://github.com/medusalix/xone,
  https://github.com/medusalix/xow, GPL-2.0): GIP LED command
  documentation corroborating xbledctl.
  PadForge's implementations are original C# and contain no code from
  these projects.

psmoveapi
  https://github.com/thp/psmoveapi
  Copyright (c) 2011, 2012 Thomas Perl
  PlayStation Move report layouts, sensor calibration decode, LED pacing
  and the read-over-USB, cache-for-Bluetooth calibration design, plus the
  EXT accessory handshake behind the Sharp Shooter and Racing Wheel,
  cross-checked against the moveonpc wiki
  (https://github.com/nitsch/moveonpc/wiki, no license published).
  PadForge's implementation is original C#.
  Licensed under the BSD 2-Clause License

$Q Super-Quick Recognizer
  https://depts.washington.edu/acelab/proj/dollar/qdollar.html
  Copyright (c) 2018-2019 Nathan Magrofuoco, Jacob O. Wobbrock,
  Radu-Daniel Vatavu, Lisa Anthony. The touchpad shape-template matcher is
  a C# re-derivation of the canonical JavaScript reference.
  Licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License (full text at the end of this file)

QR-Code-generator
  https://github.com/nayuki/QR-Code-generator
  Copyright (c) Project Nayuki. The byte-mode QR encoder behind the
  Dashboard's web controller card is a C# port of this reference
  implementation (PadForge.Services.QrCode).
  Licensed under the MIT License

SAxense
  https://apps.sdore.me/SAxense (https://github.com/egormanga/SAxense)
  By egormanga. DualSense Bluetooth audio research: the multiplexed
  packet transport the controller speaker stream rides on. PadForge's
  implementation is original C#.
  Licensed under MPL-2.0

SDL3
  https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL
  Licensed under the zlib License

SDL_GameControllerDB
  https://github.com/mdqinc/SDL_GameControllerDB
  Community gamepad mapping database. PadForge's bundled
  gamecontrollerdb_padforge.txt extends it.
  Licensed under the zlib License

SIPSorcery
  https://github.com/sipsorcery-org/sipsorcery
  Copyright (c) 2006–2026 Aaron Clauson
  The STUN Binding message layout, the 0x2112A442 magic cookie and the
  XOR-MAPPED-ADDRESS decode behind Remote Link's NAT traversal, vendored
  from its STUN sources (STUNHeader.cs, STUNMessage.cs,
  STUNXORAddressAttribute.cs).
  Licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License, with the additional use
  restriction in section 2 of its LICENSE.md (both at the end of this file)

SteamControllerSinger
  https://github.com/Roboron3042/SteamControllerSinger
  Copyright (c) 2015 Pila, fork by Roboron3042. The Steam Controller
  (2015) haptic feature-report layout and note-period math.
  Licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License (same conditions as reproduced
  in full below for BthPS3)

SteamHapticsSinger
  https://github.com/CrazyCritic89/SteamHapticsSinger
  Copyright (c) 2015-2016 Pila, Copyright (c) 2022-2026 Crazy, AAGaming.
  The Steam Controller 2026 / Steam Deck LFO-tone haptic report layout,
  gain and drive-frequency tables.
  Licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License (same conditions as reproduced
  in full below for BthPS3)

SteamKit2
  https://github.com/SteamRE/SteamKit
  Copyright (C) 2018 Ryan Stecker & SteamRE Team
  .NET Steam network client for the Steam Workshop controller-config
  import. Connects over an anonymous session and ships unmodified
  inside the executable as SteamKit2.dll. Source code for the shipped
  assembly is available at the project page above.
  Licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License v2.1 only
  (full text below)

TriggerEffectGenerator
  https://gist.github.com/Nielk1/6d54cc2c00d2201ccb8c2720ad7538db
  Copyright (c) 2021-2022 John "Nielk1" Klein
  The DualSense adaptive-trigger effect layouts and zone bitmap packing,
  reproduced in C#.
  Licensed under the MIT License

usbip-win2
  https://github.com/vadimgrn/usbip-win2
  Copyright (c) 2021-2026, Vadym Hrynchyshyn
  HIDMaestro.Core.dll carries the upstream 0.9.8.1 installers for x64
  and ARM64, unmodified, with drivers Microsoft signed, and installs the
  one matching the machine the first time a composite USB controller is
  created. It is the USB transport for those controllers. Any other
  controller type installs nothing from it.
  Licensed under the BSD 2-Clause License (full text at the end of this file)

Valve Steam Controller CAD
  https://gitlab.steamos.cloud/SteamHardware/SteamController (2026 pad)
  Valve's March 2016 Steam Controller CAD release (2015 pad)
  Copyright 2016 and 2026 Valve Corporation
  The Steam Controller (2015) and Steam Controller (2026) 3D models are
  meshed from Valve's published STEP files. PadForge is not associated
  with or endorsed by Valve.
  Licensed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0

Vosk
  https://alphacephei.com/vosk/ (https://github.com/alphacep/vosk-api)
  By Alpha Cephei Inc. Offline speech recognition for voice macros:
  hears the registered phrases and routes everything else to an unknown
  bucket. Ships as the native libvosk library inside the executable, with
  the recognition model, which is unpacked to a cache under the TEMP folder
  on first use. The x64 libvosk.dll is the one the Vosk package carries.
  The ARM64 libvosk.dll is built from Vosk 0.3.38 by
  tools/build-libvosk-arm64.sh, which is Alpha Cephei's own Windows ARM64
  recipe (vosk-api 1b308a30), because no ARM64 binary is published.
  Licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (full text below)

Windows MIDI Services
  https://github.com/microsoft/MIDI
  Licensed under MIT License

WPF UI
  https://github.com/lepoco/wpfui
  Licensed under MIT License

xbledctl
  https://github.com/Leclowndu93150/xbledctl
  By Leclowndu93150. The Xbox Guide button LED writer derives its
  \\.\XboxGIP packet layout, wire constants, and device-discovery
  sequence from this project.
  Licensed under the MIT License

Zacksly Icon Pack
  https://zacksly.itch.io/
  By Zacksly. PadForge's stick and trigger tab icon geometry derives from
  the pack's Xbox Series icons.
  Licensed under CC BY 3.0

Zergatul.Obs.InputOverlay
  https://github.com/Zergatul/Zergatul.Obs.InputOverlay
  Copyright (c) 2021 Igor Budzhak. The mouse artwork in the
  Keyboard + Mouse visualization is rendered from this project's
  mouse.svg (PadForge.App/Views/MouseArt.g.cs).
  Licensed under the MIT License

ZstdSharp
  https://github.com/oleg-st/ZstdSharp
  Copyright (c) 2021 Oleg Stepanischev
  Zstandard decompression SteamKit2 uses for Steam depot chunks.
  A C# port of the zstd compression library. Ships unmodified inside
  the executable as ZstdSharp.dll.
  Licensed under the MIT License

Special Thanks
  TechAntohere (https://github.com/TechAntohere, u/Idkiamaguy645)
  Shared his DualSense Bluetooth findings and testing, and pointed
  PadForge to the working speaker recipe.

